Ladybird excludes the line records and inline placeholders representing
interrupting blocks from scrollable overflow. Each block contributes
through its transformed box instead. The stored inline geometry still
supplies inline painting and client rectangles.

Blink’s ScrollableOverflowCalculator::AddItemsInternal distinguishes
text and line boxes from box fragments. Box fragments contribute via
ScrollableOverflowForPropagation, which applies their transforms.
Gecko’s nsIFrame::FinishAndStoreOverflow transforms each overflow area,
and nsBlockReflowContext::PlaceBlock returns that overflow at the final
frame position. nsBlockFrame::ComputeOverflowAreas distinguishes inline
lines when collecting normal-flow bounds.

WebKit’s InlineContentBuilder::computeOverflowFromBoxes excludes the
line rectangle when the line holds a block-level box. The block’s own
overflow comes from RenderBox::layoutOverflowRectForPropagation, which
applies its transform. Ladybird follows the same separation between
line-box geometry and positioned or transformed block overflow.
